WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.275
Every value in R has a type.

2
00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:07.165
In this lesson, you will meet the three most common ones:

3
00:00:07.165 --> 00:00:09.287
text, numbers, and TRUE or FALSE.

4
00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:14.237
You will also see a small mistake that almost everyone makes at the start,

5
00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:16.006
and how to fix it.

6
00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:17.420
Let's take it slowly.

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.908
Here are our three notes from before:

8
00:00:21.908 --> 00:00:23.398
character, numeric, and logical.

9
00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:25.260
Let's look at each one.

10
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.541
First, character.

11
00:00:29.541 --> 00:00:33.244
Under the note, I wrote a name inside quotation marks.

12
00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:35.836
The quotes tell R: this is text.

13
00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:40.280
Without quotes, R would think it is the name of something else.

14
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.442
Next, numeric.

15
00:01:14.442 --> 00:01:17.650
A number, like thirty for an age, needs no quotes.

16
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.820
R knows it is a number, and you can do math with it.

17
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.341
Now the logical type.

18
00:01:55.341 --> 00:01:58.037
Logical values are only TRUE or FALSE.

19
00:01:58.037 --> 00:02:01.889
We get them when we ask R a question, like:

20
00:02:01.889 --> 00:02:04.200
is twenty five equal to fifty?

21
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.548
I typed twenty five, one equals sign, fifty.

22
00:02:13.548 --> 00:02:15.952
And R shows an error in red.

23
00:02:15.952 --> 00:02:18.356
Please don't worry when you see red.

24
00:02:18.356 --> 00:02:20.760
It is R's way of helping us.

25
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.533
The problem is the single equals sign.

26
00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:33.046
In R, one equals sign means assign a value.

27
00:02:33.046 --> 00:02:36.560
To compare two values, we need two equals signs.

28
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.663
So I write fifty, two equals signs, fifty.

29
00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:48.811
Run it, and R says TRUE.

30
00:02:48.811 --> 00:02:50.600
Fifty is equal to fifty.

31
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.814
Then fifty, two equals signs, twenty five. R says FALSE.

32
00:03:02.814 --> 00:03:04.420
They are not equal.

33
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.600
So remember:

34
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:20.600
text in quotes, numbers without quotes, and two equals signs to compare. Very well done.

